# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD runs hs-start.sh, which boots rsyslog/cron/smbd/nmbd/
# ircd-irc2, starts sshd, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemons (samba on :445, sshd on :22, ircd) are ALREADY RUNNING when
#     the agent starts — the service and behavioural probes exercise live
#     subsystems, and "fixed the config but never restarted the service" stays
#     detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting smbd/sshd cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART the affected service (e.g. smbd
# after editing smb.conf), not merely start it if absent.
